 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "One week in, the climate summit is stuck on oil, gas and coal. Why?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "COP thirty-one's first week in Antalya, Turkey, ended Friday. Observers told Reuters big fossil fuel producers and consumers resist any deal with firm new targets or a shift from oil, gas and coal. The United States skipped the talks again."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Host Turkey's plan: electricity at thirty-five percent of world energy use by twenty thirty-five. Negotiations chief Chris Bowen says that share rose from seventeen percent in two thousand five to twenty-three today. Reuters reports the plan does not require clean power."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Brazil, last year's host, presented a voluntary roadmap away from fossil fuels. Climate Home News reports India, Nigeria and Germany backed it. U.N. chief António Guterres wants progress from every country by twenty twenty-eight. Bowen expects a first draft deal early next week."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the final COP thirty-one deal name fossil fuels? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
